 and the default Apps submenu holds only apps, so no app competes with a menu row inside one sorted list. With the bias reset to -5 in a scratch copy of the head MenuModel.js, 544 queries (every letter, 234 two-letter queries, 12 words; at the root and in Apps; five apps) gave the same rows and Enter target as the PR. Against base 1e433732, 52 of them changed rows or divider and 46 changed the Enter target. The bias decides order only where apps and menu rows share a list: a menu extension that adds a non-app entry to Apps, or direct searchScore callers (the tests). The PR gives both changes as fixes; a maintainer may want to keep one mechanism, or a test that shows what the bias still governs.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":702},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js","kind":"file","line":377},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-SJ7P","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-TKDP","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"medium","title":"Opinion (my own run, not engine-verified): the pinning alone decides the display order; the -100 bias changes no visible row","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml:rebuildDisplay","shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js:searchScore"],"scenario":"root search for 'system' with btop installed (Keywords system), and 'terminal' with a terminal app whose GenericName is Terminal: Enter runs the app instead of the exact-label System / Setup > Defaults > Terminal entry"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"Still holds against the new baseline. Baseline SJ7P lets an app win only against an EQUAL menu row; an exact label (tier 0) beats a name or keyword match (tier 40). With the PR, at the root with the shipped menu: `system` puts apps.btop (Keywords system;process;task) above the root entry labelled exactly System, so Enter opens btop++. Here the base order came from TKDP's current-before-deeper rule. `terminal` with a terminal app whose GenericName is Terminal (Alacritty, or the shipped foot) puts the app above Setup > Defaults > Terminal (omarchy-menu.jsonc:163), the base Enter target, and Install > Terminal. Here the base order came from SJ7P's tiers. In both, Enter now runs the app. Identical on upstream 9c5482c5 vs the PR applied. The pinning decides it: with the bias at -5 the app still comes first. The mirror's witness pins only the score form ('update', menumodel-replay.test.mjs:1425). The PR discloses the general tradeoff, not the exact-label case. A maintainer decision is needed.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":711},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js","kind":"file","line":377},{"id":"default/omarchy/omarchy-menu.jsonc","kind":"file","line":34},{"id":"default/omarchy/omarchy-menu.jsonc","kind":"file","line":163},{"id":"test/node/menumodel-replay.test.mjs","kind":"file","line":1425},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-SJ7P","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-TKDP","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"medium","title":"Question: should a keyword-only app match beat an exact-label menu entry?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Exact-label menu entry vs keyword-only app\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml:rebuildDisplay"],"scenario":"root search 'tu' with one installed app matching: the divider between direct children (setup) and deeper entries (install.tui) is no longer drawn"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"Still holds. For root `tu` with VS Code installed, base gives `setup | install.tui ...` and head gives `apps.code | setup install.tui ...`: the current-menu rows and the deeper rows now share one section under a single divider. The PR says only \"with the divider following them\". Baseline TKDP had a divider between current-menu and deeper matches whenever both exist. Our TKDP rewrite (\"one divider separates the apps from all menu entries\") and the witness at menumodel-replay.test.mjs:1406 codify the new form. That is our reading, not the author's statement.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":705},{"id":"test/node/menumodel-replay.test.mjs","kind":"file","line":1406},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-TKDP","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"medium","title":"Question: is dropping the direct/deeper divider whenever an app matches intended?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Divider placement with direct, deeper and app matches all present\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml:rebuildDisplay"],"scenario":"root search 'e' with 200 installed apps: index of the first menu row in the result list"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"Every matching app now precedes every menu row. In my scratch run at 0f17f438 with synthetic apps that all match `e`, the first menu row moved from index 0 (base 1e433732) to index 20 with 20 apps and to index 200 with 200 apps. The PR screenshots show one-app cases only.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":711},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-TKDP","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"low","title":"Question: with many installed apps, do short queries bury every menu entry?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Burial at scale\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js:searchScore"],"scenario":"property: for every tier value and kind, max app score*1000+depth*25+order < min menu/link score*1000"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"The invariant \"exceeds every match tier\" exists only in a comment (the mirror's SJ7P now states it too). A future tier at 98 or above would let a menu row outrank an app wherever both share a sorted list: a non-app entry an extension adds to Apps, or a direct searchScore caller. The root display would not change, because the pinning orders it. The MC/DC replay pins today's values, not the invariant.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js","kind":"file","line":377},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-SJ7P","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"low","title":"Question: does the -100 bias stay above every tier if a tier >= 98 is added? (opinion: name the constant)","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Tier-gap invariant property test\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"detail":"testResults: ingested, current, 69 passed / 0 failed / 0 skipped (8 tagged tests, all joined). The baseline run had 68; the extra result is our test 'Menu.qml rebuildDisplay search ranking with installed apps (PR #12223 witnesses)'. menu-compositor-test.sh and menu-acceptance-test.sh appear in review.tests with outcome passed. Of the 73 cells, 39 are observed_pass, 30 not_linked (no test tagged with that class) and 4 suppressed: external_call_timeout_bounded on MQ37, RGCV, W17G and Y58B, each with a recorded obligation_suppression reason in the base data. Neither not_linked nor suppressed cells are tested evidence. SJ7P (4 passed) and TKDP (3 passed) are observed_pass as changed as intended. I re-ran the two node suites at 0f17f438 (30 pass, 1 skip: #10601 needs Qt) and menu-test.sh (exit 0).","refs":[{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-compositor-test.sh","kind":"file","line":1},{"id":"test/